    "extraction_notes": [
      "Transfer, output, on-resistance, normalized-temperature, capacitance, and gate-charge curves are approximate digitizations from the typical-characteristics figures on p. 3; axes and stated test conditions are retained.",
      "The transfer figure labels its horizontal axis as VDS-GATE VOLTAGE; it is interpreted as VGS because the figure is titled Transfer Characteristics and plots drain current against gate voltage.",
      "The dynamic-parameter table publishes Ciss = 247 pF, Coss = 34 pF, and Crss = 19.5 pF at the shared condition VDS = 30 V, VGS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz. The capacitance curves on p. 3 are separately retained as digitized typical traces over VDS = 0 to 20 V.",
      "The switching table publishes Qg = 6 nC, Qgs = 1 nC, Qgd = 1.3 nC, Qrr = 6.99 nC, and trr = 32.6 ns. The gate-charge curve is retained, but the supplied schema has no dedicated fields for these switching quantities.",
      "The static table publishes IDSS maximum 1 uA at VDS = 60 V and VGS = 0 V, and 100 uA at VDS = 20 V, VGS = 0 V, Tj = 150 degC. It also publishes VSD maximum 1.2 V and IS maximum 3 A; these values are not represented by dedicated schema fields.",
      "The thermal data publishes RthetaJA = 104 K/W maximum at Ta = 25 degC; no RthetaJC value is published. The supplied schema has no dedicated thermal-resistance fields.",
      "Safe operating area, maximum continuous drain current versus ambient temperature, and normalized transient thermal impedance plots were examined but are not included as model-fitting curves because the supplied schema has no dedicated SOA or thermal-impedance fields."
    ],
    "omission_reason": "The supplied schema has no dedicated fields for gate charge, reverse-recovery charge/time, leakage, maximum body-diode current, switching timing, thermal resistance, safe operating area, or transient thermal impedance; those published values are retained only in extraction_notes."
  },
